# Learner portal — clickable containers

When a list item, card, or glance tile navigates somewhere, the **entire container** is the hit target.

## Do

- Wrap the row in `Link` with `className={styles.rowLink}` (or `styles.glanceLink` for dashboard glance tiles).
- Keep status chips / CTA text (`styles.linkish` with “→”) inside the container as visual affordance only — not the sole click target.
- Use a plain `styles.row` (non-link) only when there is **no** destination (e.g. locked modules, completed reviews without a learner record URL, OTJ status-only rows).

## Don’t

- Put a small text-only `Link` (`styles.linkish`) inside a static `styles.row` as the only way to navigate.
- Nest interactive links inside a `rowLink` container.

## Pattern

```tsx
<li>
  <Link href={href} className={styles.rowLink}>
    <div className={styles.rowMain}>
      <strong>{title}</strong>
      <span>{detail}</span>
    </div>
    <div className={styles.rowEnd}>
      <LearnerStatusChip tone="amber">Open</LearnerStatusChip>
      <span className={styles.linkish}>{ctaLabel} →</span>
    </div>
  </Link>
</li>
```
